Z||000002||Dave Gunsul||06-08-2001||05:50 PM||||I am sooo glad that someone has FINALLY said that!! I keep reading about all these wimps<BR>wanting power steering and I keep thinking that something has to wrong with their car because the two I own and all the ones i've ever driven have felt so good without power steering. The good road feel was one of the biggest reasons that I got into Fieros in the first place!<BR>Hmmm, was that a rant??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||14
Z||000003||rockcrawl||06-08-2001||06:15 PM||||I like the stock Fiero steering feel too, but slap on some 9" wide rims with adapters/spacers to match the look and width of a body kit, and then see how you like manual steering. The Fiero has a pretty horible scrub radius as is, and this stuff only makes it worse. I wouldn't even consider putting power steering on a stock Fiero, but it will almost be a neccesity with my TR replica.<BR> By adjusting the hydraulic pressure, you can make the power assist almost un-noticeable, but I suppose the fluid dampening will still take away some of the "road feel".<P>A related note on comparing the Fiero to an F-body. I just bought a Fiero from a guy that now has a new TA. He says he likes the straight-line power of the TA , but he wishes it could handle the turns as well as the Fiero. I was happy to hear him say that.||||reg||7
Z||000004||Fformula88||06-08-2001||06:31 PM||||Power steering can be fine.  Some cars, mostly sportier ones tend to have units that let in a decent amount of road feel.  They don't "over-assist".  Then there is my mom's Buick!  I cannot stand the steering on it.  No feel at all!  I certainly wouldn't want it in the Fiero.  Its also too bad the Miata is no longer available without it.||||reg||1
